 "notes": "SOURCE FILE WAS TRUNCATED: the delivered PDF (9,318,016 bytes) is an incomplete download — no xref/trailer/catalog/page-tree and only the first ~106 content pages survived (physical pages up to ~p71). I recovered it by scanning surviving objects with PyMuPDF, pairing each text content stream with its adjacent /Font resource dict, appending a synthetic Catalog+Pages tree, and repairing with qpdf; the reconstructed doc extracts real text via the fonts' ToUnicode CMaps (not OCR). Chapters 3+ (Enterobacterales trend tables, R&D chapters) fall beyond the truncation point and could NOT be read.\n\nVALUES ARE POOLED FROM COUNTS: All %S values were computed by summing the S/tested counts across the OPD+Ward+ICU columns of the Chapter-2 specimen-wise tables (Section B), so they are exact pooled percentages, not read-off %. Sources by organism: E. coli / K. pneumoniae / A. baumannii / Salmonella Typhi = BLOOD (Tables 2.7, 2.8, 2.9, 2.10); P. aeruginosa = URINE (Table 2.13, no blood table survived); S. aureus = PUS/EXUDATES (Table 2.17); E. faecalis / E. faecium = URINE (Tables 2.14, 2.15). Salmonella Typhi table had only OPD+Ward columns (n=1061). Denominators validate against Table 1.2 isolat",
